{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-005", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh secures $336 mn China loan for Mongla Port", "content": "Bangladesh has signed a $335.78 million concessional loan with China Exim Bank to expand and modernise Mongla Port, its second-largest seaport. \nThe 2 per cent loan is repayable over 20 years with a five-year grace period and will fund two container terminals, modern machinery and yards. \nThe Tk 4,068.23 crore project is due by December 2028 as Bangladesh seeks to develop Mongla as a regional hub. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-secures-336-mn-china-loan-for-mongla-port-314246-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-14-006", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.67, "keywords": ["decline", "slow", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s polyester, viscose yarn face persistent payment issue", "content": "India’s polyester and viscose yarn markets stayed weak as sluggish demand, falling crude oil and tight payments hit trade, with Surat posting declines.\nLudhiana polyester-cotton and polyester yarn prices were stable; viscose eased in Surat but held in Mumbai as festive demand lagged last year.\nNorth Indian cotton rose on firmer ICE futures, slower arrivals and farmers withholding stocks.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-polyester-viscose-yarn-face-persistent-payment-issue-314254-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "nike-2026-10-14-007", "date": "2026-10-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["nike"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Nike’s $2.5 bn pace plan: Which Asian suppliers face pressure?", "content": "Nike’s Q1 FY2027 revenue fell 4 per cent to $11.21 billion, with full-year revenue forecast to drop by a high-single-digit percentage.\nGreater China dropped 22 per cent and Converse 28 per cent; Dunk, Jordan and Sportswear weakened, while performance categories grew.\nPace targets $2.5 billion in savings by fiscal 2031, shifting supplier focus to productivity, flexibility and technical expertise.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/nike-s-2-5-bn-pace-plan-which-asian-suppliers-face-pressure--314252-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
